      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While inflammation is likely a contributing factor, painful swelling on the calf could also be a sign of potential issues like DVT (deep vein thrombosis), blood clots, or nerve compression, which may not be resolved by elevation or over-the-counter pain relievers. These complications can be serious and require medical attention to prevent more severe consequences. I would strongly recommend consulting your surgeon or primary care doctor to minimize the risk of any potential complications.",
      "source": "target",
